[{"id":"smq-year2-2.24-q1","number":1,"question":"<p>Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for each of the following:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x(x-1)^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x^2(2x+7)^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=4x(7-x)^4\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=(x+2)^2(3x+1)^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=(3-x)^2(2x+9)^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\sqrt{2x+5}(4x+1)^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=(\\frac1x-2x)(\\frac1{x^3}+\\frac2{x^5})\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=x\\times2(x-1)+(x-1)^2=2x(x-1)+(x-1)^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=x^2\\times4(2x+7)+2x\\times(2x+7)^2=4x^2(2x+7)+2x(2x+7)^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=4x\\times-4(7-x)^3+4(7-x)^4=-16x(7-x)^3+4(7-x)^4\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=9(x+2)^2(3x+1)^2+2(x+2)(3x+1)^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=(3-x)^2\\times2\\times3(2x+9)^2-2(3-x)(2x+9)^3=6(3-x)^2(2x+9)^2-2(3-x)(2x+9)^3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">f)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{dy}{dx} =\\sqrt{2x+5}\\times8(4x+1)+2\\times\\tfrac12(2x+5)^{-1/2}(4x+1)^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =8\\sqrt{2x+5}(4x+1)+(2x+5)^{-1/2}(4x+1)^2\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">g)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=(\\tfrac1x-2x)(-3x^{-4}-10x^{-6})+(-x^{-2}-2)(\\tfrac1{x^3}+\\tfrac2{x^5})\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.24-q2","number":2,"question":"<p>Three students attempt to find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac d{dx}((x^2-1)(x^3+5))\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Identify the correct version and spot the error(s) in the other two:</p><p><u>Student A:</u></p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(x^2-1)(x^3+5)=x^5-x^3+5x^2+5\" data-display=\"true\"></span><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=5x^6-3x^2+10x\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p><u>Student B:</u></p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=(2x)(x^3+5)+(x^2-1)(3x^2)=5x^4-3x^2+10x\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p><u>Student C:</u></p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=2x\\times3x^2=6x^3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","steps":["<p>Student A: incorrectly multiplied out the brackets. Incorrectly differentiated the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^5\" data-display=\"false\"></span> term.</p>","<p>Student B: Correct method.</p>","<p>Student C: incorrectly multiplied the two differentials of the two brackets together without applying the product rule.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.24-q3","number":3,"question":"<p>Differentiate the following:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x\\ln x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\sqrt x\\tan x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\sin x\\cos x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\cos x\\ln x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=2^x\\sin x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=(x^2+1)\\ln x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=x\\times\\frac1x+\\ln x=1+\\ln x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=x^{1/2}\\sec^2x+\\frac12x^{-1/2}\\tan x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\sin x\\times-\\sin x+\\cos x\\cos x=\\cos^2x-\\sin^2x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac1x\\cos x-\\sin x\\ln x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=2^x\\cos x+\\ln2\\times2^x\\sin x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">f)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{x^2+1}x+2x\\ln x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.24-q4","number":4,"question":"<p>Differentiate and fully factorise the following:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=xe^x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x^24^x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=e^x\\tan x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=2^x\\sin x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=(x^2-12)e^{-2x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=e^{4x}\\sin2x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=xe^x+e^x=e^x(x+1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=(\\ln4)x^24^x+2x\\times4^x=4^xx(x\\ln4+2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=e^x\\sec^2x+e^x\\tan x=e^x(\\sec^2x+\\tan x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=2^x\\cos x+\\ln2\\times2^x\\sin x=2^x(\\cos x+\\ln2\\sin x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=(x^2-12)\\times-2e^{-2x}+2xe^{-2x}=-2e^{-2x}(x^2-12)=-2e^{-2x}(x-4)(x+3)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">f)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=2\\cos2x\\ e^{4x}+\\sin2x\\times4e^{4x}=2e^{4x}(\\cos2x+2\\sin2x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.24-q5","number":5,"question":"<p>Find the equation of the tangent line to the curve at the given point, giving your answers in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=mx+c\" data-display=\"false\"></span>:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x^3(x+2)^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x^5\\sqrt{3x+10}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=(x^2-x+4)e^x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=2x^3(x+2)+3x^2(x+2)^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=9\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=1}=6+27=33\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y-9=33(x-1)\\Rightarrow y=33x-24\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac32x^5(3x+10)^{-1/2}+5x^4\\sqrt{3x+10}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=128\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=2}=332\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y-128=332(x-2)\\Rightarrow y=332x-536\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=(x^2-x+4)e^x+(2x-1)e^x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=0}=4-1=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y-4=3(x-0)\\Rightarrow y=3x+4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.24-q6","number":6,"question":"<p>Fully factorise each of the following:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4x^2+2x^2(x+1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3(2x-1)^5-(x+1)(2x-1)^4\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4(3x+1)^3+(x+2)(3x+1)^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac13(6x+5)^3+(x-1)(6x+5)^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac12(1-x)^{-5}+4(1-x)^{-6}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"4(4x+1)^3(3x-1)+9(3x-1)^2(4x+1)^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2x^2[2+(x+1)]=2x^2(x+3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(2x-1)^4[3(2x-1)-(x+1)]=(2x-1)^4[6x-3-x-1]=(2x-1)^4(5x-4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3x+1)^2[4(3x+1)+(x+2)]=(3x+1)^2[12x+4+x+2]=(3x+1)^2(13x+6)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac13(6x+5)^2[(6x+5)+3(x-1)]=\\frac13(6x+5)^2[6x+5+3x-3]=\\frac13(6x+5)^2(9x+2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">e)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac1{2(1-x)^5}+\\frac4{(1-x)^6}=\\frac1{2(1-x)^6}[(1-x)+8]=\\frac1{2(1-x)^6}(9-x)=\\frac{9-x}{2(1-x)^6}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">f)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(3x-1)(4x+1)^2[4(4x+1)+9(3x-1)]=(3x-1)(4x+1)^2[16x+4+27x-9]=(3x-1)(4x+1)^2(43x-5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.24-q7","number":7,"question":"<p>Solve each of the following:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2(x+1)^3+(x-1)(x+1)^2=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac13(2x+1)^{-2}+(2x+1)^{-3}=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"5(7x-1)^3(x-1)-3(x-1)^2(7x-1)^2=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(x+1)^2[2(x+1)+(x-1)]=0\\Rightarrow(x+1)^2[2x+2+x-1]=0\\Rightarrow(x+1)^2(3x+1)=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-\\frac13\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac1{3(2x+1)^2}+\\frac1{(2x+1)^3}=0\\Rightarrow\\frac1{3(2x+1)^3}[(2x+1)+3]=0\\Rightarrow\\frac{2x+4}{3(2x+1)^3}=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(7x-1)^2(x-1)[5(7x-1)-3(x-1)]=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"(7x-1)^2(x-1)[35x-5-3x+3]=0\\Rightarrow(7x-1)^2(x-1)(32x-2)=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac17\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac1{16}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.24-q8","number":8,"question":"<p>The curve shown below is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x^3(3x-5)^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><figure class=\"diagram\"><img src=\"assets/smq-2.24/questions/assets/diagrams/224-q8.png\" alt=\"Original mathematical diagram\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure><p>A local maximum value is at the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the coordinates of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li><li><p>State the coordinates of the other stationary points.</p></li><li><p>State the values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for which the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x^3(3x-5)^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has three unique solutions.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=6x^3(3x-5)+3x^2(3x-5)^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Stat pt when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"6x^3(3x-5)+3x^2(3x-5)^2=0\\Rightarrow3x^2(3x-5)[2x+(3x-5)]=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"3x^2(3x-5)[5x-5]=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac53\" data-display=\"false\"></span> or1 so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\frac53,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0&lt;y&lt;4\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.24-q9","number":9,"question":"<p>For each of the following, differentiate and fully factorise:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x(x+3)^7\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=(x-3)(2x+1)^4\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=5x(2x+1)^4\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=(1+x^2)e^{2x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=7x(x+3)^6+(x+3)^7=(x+3)^6[7x+(x+3)]=(x+3)^6(8x+3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{dy}{dx} =8(x-3)(2x+1)^3+(2x+1)^4\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =(2x+1)^3[8(x-3)+(2x+1)]\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =(2x+1)^3[8x-24+2x+1]=(2x+1)^3(10x-23)\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{dy}{dx} =40x(2x+1)^3+5(2x+1)^4=(2x+1)^3[40x+5(2x+1)]\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =(2x+1)^3(50x+5)=5(2x+1)^3(10x+1)\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{dy}{dx} =2(1+x^2)e^{2x}+2xe^{2x}=e^{2x}[2(1+x^2)+2x]\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =e^{2x}[2x^2+2x+2]=2e^{2x}(x^2+x+1)\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.24-q10","number":10,"question":"<p>A curve is given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=4000xe^{-2x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the stationary point of the curve.</p></li><li><p>Determine its type.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=-8000xe^{-2x}+4000e^{-2x}=-4000e^{-2x}(2x-1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Stat pt when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac12\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\frac12,\\frac{2000}e)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=-8000e^{-2x}+8000e^{-2x}(2x-1)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}\\right|_{x=1/2}=-8000e^{-1}&lt;0\\text{ so maximum}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.24-q11","number":11,"question":"<p>The number of employees <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, in a company in the first 12 months may be modelled by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=150-3t\\sin(\\frac\\pi6t)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the number of months after 1st January.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find the number of employees predicted by the model on 1st January.</p></li><li><p>Find an expression for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dt}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Find the rate of change in the number of employees predicted by the model on 1st April.</p></li><li><p>Interpret your result in part c) giving your answer in context.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>150employees</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dt}=-\\frac\\pi2t\\cos\\frac\\pi6t-3\\sin\\frac\\pi6t\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{dy}{dt}\\right|_{t=3}=-\\frac{3\\pi}2\\cos\\frac\\pi2-3\\sin\\frac\\pi2=-3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">d)</h3><p>On exactly1st April the company is losing3 employees per day.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.24-q12","number":12,"question":"<p>Find the equation of the tangent line to the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x^4e^{2x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Give your answer in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y+pe^2x+qe^2=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=2x^4e^{2x}+4x^3e^{2x}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{dy}{dy}\\right|_{x=1}=2e^2+4e^2=6e^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=e^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y-e^2=6e^2(x-1)\\Rightarrow y-e^2=6e^2x-6e^2\\Rightarrow y-6e^2x+5e^2=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.24-q13","number":13,"question":"<p>A curve is given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x\\ln x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Find the stationary point and determine its type.</p>","steps":["<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=x\\times\\frac1x+\\ln x=1+\\ln x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Stat pt when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"1+\\ln x=0\\Rightarrow\\ln x=-1\\Rightarrow x=e^{-1}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(e^{-1},-e^{-1})\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=\\frac1x\\text{ so }\\left.\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}\\right|_{x=e^{-1}}=e&gt;0\\text{ so a minimum}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.24-q14","number":14,"question":"<p>A curve is given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=e^{-x}\\sin x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\geq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that the curve has a stationary point at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\frac\\pi4,\\frac{\\sqrt2}2e^{-\\pi/4})\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Determine its type.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=e^{-x}\\cos x-e^{-x}\\sin x=e^{-x}(\\cos x-\\sin x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. At <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac\\pi4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>,</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=e^{-\\pi/4}(\\cos\\tfrac\\pi4-\\sin\\tfrac\\pi4)=e^{-\\pi/4}(\\tfrac{\\sqrt2}2-\\tfrac{\\sqrt2}2)=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So stat pt at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac\\pi4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"e^{-\\pi/4}\\sin\\tfrac\\pi4=\\tfrac{\\sqrt2}2e^{-\\pi/4}\\text{ so }(\\tfrac\\pi4,\\tfrac{\\sqrt2}2e^{-\\pi/4})\\text{ as req.}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2} =e^{-x}(-\\sin x-\\cos x)-e^{-x}(\\cos x-\\sin x)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =e^{-x}(-\\sin x-\\cos x-\\cos x+\\sin x)=-2e^{-x}\\cos x\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}\\right|_{x=\\pi/4}=-2e^{-\\pi/4}\\cos\\tfrac\\pi4=-\\sqrt2e^{-\\pi/4}&lt;0\\text{ so max}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.24-q15","number":15,"question":"<p><strong>Prerequisite knowledge for Q15: Geometric Sequences</strong> A curve is given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=10e^x\\cos x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\geq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Show that the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> coordinates of the stationary points of the curve satisfy the equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\tan x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol><p>The <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-values of the stationary points satisfy a geometric sequence,</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li><p>find the value of the common ratio <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=-10e^x\\sin x+10e^x\\cos x=10e^x(\\cos x-\\sin x)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Stat pt when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"10e^x(\\cos x-\\sin x)=0\\text{ but }e^x\\ne0\\Rightarrow\\cos x-\\sin x=0\\Rightarrow\\sin x=\\cos x\\Rightarrow\\tan x=1\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>For <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\geq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, stat pts at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac\\pi4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{5\\pi}4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{9\\pi}4\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\ldots\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=\\ldots,5\\sqrt2e^{\\pi/4},5\\sqrt2e^{5\\pi/4},5\\sqrt2e^{9\\pi/4},\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"r=-e^\\pi\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.24-q16","number":16,"question":"<p>Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f'(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for each of the following:</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=e^{10x^2}\\sin(2x^3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=5^{x^2}\\cos(1-x^2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=(x^2+1)^3\\ln(x^2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f'(x)=6x^2e^{10x^2}\\cos(2x^3)+20xe^{10x^2}\\sin(2x^3)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\mathrm f'(x) =2x\\times5^{x^2}\\sin(1-x^2)+2x\\ln5\\times5^{x^2}\\cos(1-x^2)\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =2x5^{x^2}\\sin(1-x^2)+2x(\\ln5)5^{x^2}\\cos(1-x^2)\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f'(x)=\\frac{2x}{x^2}(x^2+1)^3+6x(x^2+1)^2\\ln(x^2)=\\frac2x(x^2+1)^3+6x(x^2+1)^2\\ln(x^2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.24-q17","number":17,"question":"<p><strong>Prerequisite knowledge for Q17: Points of Inflection</strong> Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=2^{3x^2}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is convex (concave upwards) for all values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\ln2\\times6x\\times2^{3x^2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}=\\ln2\\times36x^2\\times2^{3x^2}+6\\ln2\\times2^{3x^2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> for all <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span> since <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^2\\geq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Therefore convex for all <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.24-q18","number":18,"question":"<p>Show that the curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=(5-2x)\\ln(x+1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> has a stationary point at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\approx1.04\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\frac{5-2x}{x+1}-2\\ln(x+1)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Stat pt when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x\\approx1.04}=\\frac{5-2\\times1.04}{1.04+1}-2\\ln(1.04+1)=0.0005540\\ldots\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x\\approx0.94}=\\frac{5-2\\times0.94}{0.94+1}-2\\ln(0.94+1)&gt;0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x\\approx1.14}=\\frac{5-2\\times1.14}{1.14+1}-2\\ln(1.14+1)&lt;0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>So the gradient before the point is positive and the gradient after the point is negative.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.24-q19","number":19,"question":"<p>For each of the following curves find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, find the coordinates of any stationary points.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x^2e^x\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=(3x-1)^4(3x^2+1)^5\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\sqrt x(x-1)^2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=x^2e^x+2xe^x=xe^x(x+2)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Stat pt when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"xe^x(x+2)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"e^x\\ne0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(0,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(-2,4e^{-2})\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{dy}{dx} =30x(3x-1)^4(3x^2+1)^4+12(3x-1)^3(3x^2+1)^5\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =6(3x-1)^3(3x^2+1)^4[5x(3x-1)+2(3x^2+1)]\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =6(3x-1)^3(3x^2+1)^4[15x^2-5x+6x^2+2]\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =6(3x-1)^3(3x^2+1)^4(21x^2-5x+2)\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Stat pt when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"6(3x-1)^3(3x^2+1)^4(21x^2-5x+2)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. For <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3x^2+1=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, there are no real solutions (as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x^2\\geq0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3x^2+1\\geq1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>). For <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"21x^2-5x+2=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b^2-4ac=-143&lt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so no real solutions. So the only solution comes from <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3x-1=0\\Rightarrow x=\\frac13\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Therefore there is a stationary point at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\frac13,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\frac{dy}{dx} =2\\sqrt x(x-1)+\\tfrac12x^{-1/2}(x-1)^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =2\\sqrt x(x-1)+\\frac1{2\\sqrt x}(x-1)^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac{4x}{2\\sqrt x}(x-1)+\\frac1{2\\sqrt x}(x-1)^2\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac1{2\\sqrt x}(x-1)[4x+(x-1)]=\\frac1{2\\sqrt x}(x-1)(5x-1)\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<p>Stat pt when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac1{2\\sqrt x}(x-1)(5x-1)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. So <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=1\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac15\" data-display=\"false\"></span> therefore <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(1,0)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(\\frac15,\\frac{16}{25\\sqrt5})\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.24-q20","number":20,"question":"<p>For the curve given by <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=(y+2)\\ln(3y-5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y&gt;\\frac53\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dx}{dy}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Hence find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dx}{dy}=\\frac{3(y+2)}{3y-5}+\\ln(3y-5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"0=(y+2)\\ln(3y-5)\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=-2\" data-display=\"false\"></span> or <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"3y-5=1\\Rightarrow y=2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{dx}{dy}\\right|_{y=-2}=\\ln(-11)\\text{ not possible}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{dx}{dy}\\right|_{y=2}=12\\text{ so }\\frac{dy}{dx}=\\tfrac1{12}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.24-q21","number":21,"question":"<p>A curve has the equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x^2\\tan^3x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"-\\frac\\pi2&lt;x&lt;\\frac\\pi2\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. Show that the gradient of the curve at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\frac\\pi4\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac\\pi8(3\\pi+4)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","steps":["<p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x^2(\\tan x)^3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>.</p>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dy}{dx}=3x^2\\sec^2x(\\tan x)^2+2x(\\tan x)^3\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{dy}{dx}\\right|_{x=\\pi/4}=3\\frac{\\pi^2}{16}\\times2+2\\times\\frac\\pi4=\\frac{3\\pi^2}8+\\frac\\pi2=\\frac\\pi8(3\\pi+4)\\text{ as req.}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.24-q22","number":22,"question":"<p>The height, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\" data-display=\"false\"></span> metres, from the ground of a bungee jumper is modelled by the equation</p><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"h=10+25e^{-0.05t}(1+\\cos(\\tfrac\\pi3t))\" data-display=\"true\"></span><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\" data-display=\"false\"></span> is the time in seconds after jumping.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>State the height above the ground of the start position.</p></li><li><p>Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dh}{dt}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> and the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{dh}{dt}\" data-display=\"false\"></span> when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Explain what is happening to the bungee jumper at precisely 3 seconds.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h=10+25\\times2=60\" data-display=\"false\"></span> m.</p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{dh}{dt}=-\\frac\\pi3\\times25e^{-0.05t}\\sin(\\tfrac\\pi3t)-1.25e^{-0.05t}(1+\\cos(\\tfrac\\pi3t))\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\left.\\frac{dh}{dt}\\right|_{t=3}=0\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>When <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=3\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h=10\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so the bungee jumper has reached the minimum height which is10m above the ground.</p>"]},{"id":"smq-year2-2.24-q23","number":23,"question":"<p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=x\\sqrt{4x+3}\" data-display=\"false\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x&gt;-\\frac34\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"1\"><li><p>Find <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f'(x)\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f''(x)=\\frac{12(x+1)}{(3+4x)^{3/2}}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p></li><li><p>Find the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\" data-display=\"false\"></span>-value of the turning point and determine its nature.</p></li></ol>","steps":["<h3 class=\"part-label\">a)</h3><p><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f'(x)=2x(4x+3)^{-1/2}+\\sqrt{4x+3}\" data-display=\"false\"></span></p>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">b)</h3><span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n\\mathrm f''(x) =-4x(4x+3)^{-3/2}+2(4x+3)^{-1/2}+2(4x+3)^{-1/2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =-4x(4x+3)^{-3/2}+4(4x+3)^{-1/2}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =-\\frac{4x}{(4x+3)^{3/2}}+\\frac4{(4x+3)^{1/2}}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =-\\frac{4x}{(4x+3)^{3/2}}+\\frac{4(4x+3)}{(4x+3)^{3/2}}\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<span class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\n =\\frac{-4x+16x+12}{(4x+3)^{3/2}}=\\frac{12(x+1)}{(4x+3)^{3/2}}\\text{ as req.}\n\" data-display=\"true\"></span>","<h3 class=\"part-label\">c)</h3><p>Stat pt when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f'(x)=0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=-\\frac12\" data-display=\"false\"></span>. <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f''(-\\frac12)=6&gt;0\" data-display=\"false\"></span> so minimum point.</p>"]}]